# Compiler pass intermediates.  The passes chain
# .c -> .x (lexemes) + .tok (the same, readable) + .nam (the name
# table the later passes are filtered through) -> .ast (tree)
# + .dat (initialised data) -> .s/.as (asm) -> .o/.obj -> binary
#
# Two conventions were being squatted on and both are given back.
# ".1" through ".8" are manual section sources, and the tree and data
# files had no business holding two of them.  ".i" is post-processed
# cpp output that a person can read - C, not tokens - and ours is a
# token dump, so it is ".tok" and ".i" is left free.  This compiler
# could produce a real ".i"; lowering would make it a trainwreck to
# read, but it would be C and it would be the thing the suffix means.
#
*.x
*.tok
*.nam
*.ast
*.dat
*.s
*.as
*.asm
*.o
*.obj
*.rel
*.a
*.ast
*.pp

